course: dictionary
lesson: 4978
title: Incubator in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An incubator is a machine or box that keeps something warm so it can hatch or grow. The words around it show which kind of incubator is meant. «Eggs in incubators are safe from predators» tells you the eggs are kept in a protected, warm place.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it talks about eggs and chicks, the incubator is a warm box for eggs. If it talks about a baby born early, it is a special clear cot in hospital. If it talks about new ideas or companies, it is a place that helps them grow.
explain: Some words have several meanings, so check the clues before you choose. Swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense. If it fits the clues, you have found the right meaning.
fact: An incubator is a machine or box that keeps things warm.
fact: «Incubator» can mean an egg warmer, a hospital cot for a baby born too early, a lab box for growing cells, or a place that helps new businesses.
fact: A start-up incubator is a place or programme that helps new small companies grow.
fact: «Egg incubator» and «hospital incubator» are common phrases you will meet.
fact: You can understand the word from its context: the other words in the sentence show which meaning is used.
exercise: «Eggs in incubators are safe from predators.» What is an incubator in this sentence? | A kind of bird that lays eggs | A shop that sells eggs | *A machine that keeps eggs warm so they can hatch | A hunter that catches animals
exercise: Mia reads that a premature baby stays in an incubator until strong enough. What is the incubator here? | A kind of bird | A bed in a shop | A school trip | *A special clear cot in hospital that keeps the baby warm and safe
exercise: Sam reads that start-up incubators help new ideas. What does an incubator do for a new company? | Makes it cold and still | *Helps it grow | Turns it into an egg | Stops it from ever getting started
test: In the phrase «egg incubator», what does incubator mean? | *A warm machine that helps eggs hatch | A farm with many animals | A chicken that lays eggs | A cold box for ice cream
test: «The lab used a warm incubator to grow cells.» What is the incubator for? | Playing music | *Growing bacteria or cells | Cooking pasta | Cutting paper
exam: Which meaning fits best in «A start-up incubator helped the small company grow»? | A cold box for food | A kind of bird that lays eggs | *A place or programme that helps new small companies grow | A hunter that catches animals
